# AN ARCH LINUX MICROVM RUNNING QTILE ON AN X SERVER IN MEMORY.
#
# X11 FAMILY: the display server is `Xvfb` and the capture path is XSHM rather than
# wlr-screencopy. A microvm has no GPU; Xorg's modesetting driver has nothing to open, while
# Xvfb renders into its own process memory. MEASURED: this session reaches a real desktop and
# easystream captures it at 1024x768.
#
# THE SESSION BUS IS EXPLICIT. `dbus-daemon --session` with a named socket in the runtime
# directory, started by the session script; MEASURED without it a desktop draws "Unable to
# contact settings server" because nothing had a bus to talk to.

walkthrough "qtile microvm - QTILE captured from the console assertion"
  resolution 1024x768
  recording_resolution 1024x768

  needs arch-vmlinuz arch-initramfs arch.qcow2
  disk arch.qcow2

  boot as a microvm from kernel "arch-vmlinuz" and initramfs "arch-initramfs" with "console=ttyS0 root=/dev/vda rw rootfstype=ext4" without a display with memory 1536, waiting up to 240s

  # THE KERNEL FOUND THE DISK AND USERSPACE STARTED.
  the console will say "login"

  # AND THE SESSION IS vmuser's - PipeWire refuses root (`ConditionUser=!root`).
  the console will say "vmuser"

  # THE SESSION'S OWN PROCESS NAME, which only appears once it is running.
  the console will say "qtile"

  wait 20s

  stop the machine by killing it, waiting up to 60s
